1
00:04:34,285 --> 00:04:40,285
Jaime Reyes is a superhero whether he likes it or not.

2
00:09:08,571 --> 00:09:14,571
Blue Beetle is a action, science fiction, adventure
film directed by Ángel Manuel Soto.

3
00:13:42,857 --> 00:13:48,857
Recent college grad Jaime Reyes returns home full of aspirations for his
future, only to find that home is not quite as he left it.

4
00:18:17,142 --> 00:18:23,142
As he searches to find his purpose in the world, fate intervenes when Jaime unexpectedly finds
himself in possession of an ancient relic of alien biotechnology: the Scarab.

5
00:22:51,428 --> 00:22:57,428
Jaime Reyes / Blue Beetle, played by Xolo Mariduena.

6
00:27:25,714 --> 00:27:31,714
Jenny Kord, played by Bruna Marquezine.

7
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Victoria Kord, played by Susan Sarandon.

8
00:36:34,285 --> 00:36:40,285
Carapax, played by Raoul Max Trujillo.

9
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Milagros Reyes, played by Belissa Escobedo.

10
00:45:42,857 --> 00:45:48,857
Alberto Reyes, played by Damián Alcázar.

11
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
Blue Beetle is a 2023 American superhero film based on the DC
Comics character Jaime Reyes / Blue Beetle.

12
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
Directed by Ángel Manuel Soto and written by Gareth Dunnet-Alcocer, it
is the 14th film in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU).

13
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:31,714
Xolo Maridueña stars as Reyes, a recent college graduate who is granted
superpowers by an ancient alien relic known as the Scarab.

14
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Adriana Barraza, Damián Alcázar, Raoul Max Trujillo, Susan
Sarandon, and George Lopez also star in the film.

15
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
John Rickard and Zev Foreman produced the film for DC Films and Warner Bros.

16
01:13:08,571 --> 01:13:14,571
Development of a film featuring the Jaime Reyes version of Blue Beetle began by the
end of November 2018, with Dunnet-Alcocer attached as screenwriter.

17
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
Soto was hired to direct the film in February 2021
for the streaming service HBO Max.

18
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
Maridueña was cast that August, and the film was changed
to have a theatrical release in December.

19
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
Further casting took place in early 2022, and filming lasted from late May to mid-July at
Wilder Studios in Decatur, Georgia, as well as in El Paso, Texas, and Puerto Rico.

20
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,714
It is the first live-action superhero film with a Latino lead.

21
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Blue Beetle premiered in El Paso on August 14, 2023, and was
released in the United States on August 18.

22
01:40:34,285 --> 01:40:40,285
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and became the most-watched
film on the streaming service Max (formerly HBO Max) in the United States.

23
01:45:08,571 --> 01:45:14,571
Nevertheless, the film underperformed at the box office, grossing $130.8 million worldwide against a
production budget of $104–125 million, which made it the lowest-grossing film in the DCEU.

24
01:49:42,857 --> 01:49:48,857
Its box office performance was attributed to factors such as the 2023 Hollywood labor disputes,
the franchise's imminent reboot with the DC Universe (DCU), and Hurricane Hilary.

25
01:54:17,142 --> 01:54:23,142
An animated follow-up series set in the DCU is in development.

26
01:58:51,428 --> 01:58:57,428
The film explores themes of armor, superhero, family
relationships, family, high tech.

27
02:03:25,714 --> 02:03:31,714
The tone is thought_provoking.
